  "scope": "One disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 Kind cluster with one control-plane node and two worker nodes. A case-owned Python fixture runs on the two distinct worker nodes and exchanges one exact, harmless synthetic marker. The same server pod exposes a TLS server-auth-only comparator and an mTLS listener requiring a CA-trusted client certificate. The client verifies the server CA and DNS identity; the server checks the authorized client certificate URI identity before accepting the marker. Missing and separately untrusted client certificates are rejected, as is a trusted certificate for a different identity. Per-run CA and leaf keys are generated locally, mounted only as disposable Kubernetes Secrets, and excluded from evidence. No real training data, framework operator, external endpoint, feed, or target is used. This does not establish PyTorchJob/MPIJob/TFJob integration, certificate issuance/rotation/revocation, production identity authorization, or NetworkPolicy enforcement by a production CNI.",
